  "description": "Tennessee's newly redrawn 4th Congressional District stretches from part of Davidson County (Nashville) south to the Alabama state line. Republican incumbent Scott DesJarlais, first elected in 2010, won the August 6, 2026 Republican primary and is seeking an eighth term. The district retains a strong Republican lean (Cook PVI R+11), though the new map incorporates more urban Nashville voters. Multiple Democrats qualified for the primary, including Metro Nashville Councilmember Mike Cortese and 2024 candidate Victoria Broderick. An independent candidate also qualified. The general election will be held November 3, 2026.",
